Revision history for Ham-QSO

0.001  2026-11-07
    - Keep optional dependency paths available in temporary-directory documentation checks.
    - Expand station-log documentation, executable archiving examples and Pages publication guidance.
    - Reject malformed nested ADX, ambiguous application metadata and invalid typed exports.
    - Keep numeric clocks/ranges exact and retain every historical ADIF region period.
    - Bind logbook/schema paths, bound UTF-8 buffers and preflight durable batch imports.
    - Cache schema/context validation and make ADIF declaration export deterministic.
    - Integrated append-only station log, attributed corrections and trusted checkpoints.
    - ADIF 3.1.8 ADI/ADX import/export, typed extensions and official CC0 schemas.
    - Initial development version for ordinary two-station CW and RTTY QSO semantics.
    - Versioned Italian and IARU profiles with explicit rule/source provenance.
    - Separate preparation, observed transmission, reports, acknowledgements and closure.
    - Preserve partial/uncertain input; invalidate proof after corrections.
    - Reuse message parsers and index retained observations without duplicate JSON payloads.
    - Preserve history when selecting a peer after earlier operator actions.
    - Optional real Ham::CW/Ham::RTTY adapters without PDL.
    - CPAN packaging, CLI, examples, author checks and shared documentation website.
